WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.437
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:05.468
This is the change itself: one
instance's logins move from Windows

3
00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:09.549
to Microsoft Entra ID, first on a
test instance, then in production.

4
00:00:09.549 --> 00:00:13.587
The commands are the same both times;
only the settings file changes.

5
00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:15.451
Three rules hold it together.

6
00:00:15.451 --> 00:00:18.888
Nothing runs that a second
person didn't approve by hash.

7
00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:21.474
The way back is planned
before the cutover.

8
00:00:21.474 --> 00:00:24.822
And production's preflight
refuses to start until a real test

9
00:00:24.822 --> 00:00:28.037
stage for the same instance is
sealed in the evidence chain.

10
00:00:28.037 --> 00:00:31.610
In this module you rehearse that
whole test stage as a dry run.
